---
// Fig. for "Linear Algebra over Finite Fields": packing a claimed computation
// into a vector z = (1, x, y, w) and checking each multiplication step as
// (row A • z) × (row B • z) = (row C • z) — the shape of an R1CS constraint.
---
<svg viewBox="0 0 760 560" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;">
  <text x="380" y="26" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="16" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">constraints as dot products</text>

  <rect x="40" y="46" width="680" height="42" rx="10" fill="#111c2e" stroke="#3ab7ff" stroke-width="1.5" />
  <text x="380" y="72" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">Can a computation be checked with dot products?</text>

  <text x="380" y="108" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">SETUP</text>
  <text x="380" y="130" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">claim: x = 3, y = x &#215; x = 9 = 2, w = y &#215; x = 6 (mod 7)</text>
  <text x="380" y="152" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">pack everything into one vector z = (1, x, y, w) = (1, 3, 2, 6)</text>

  <text x="380" y="186" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">STEP 1 &#8212; constraint y = x &#215; x</text>
  <text x="380" y="210" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13.5" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">(row A)&#8226;z = (0, 1, 0, 0)&#8226;z = 3</text>
  <text x="380" y="230" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13.5" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">(row B)&#8226;z = (0, 1, 0, 0)&#8226;z = 3</text>
  <text x="380" y="250" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13.5" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">(row C)&#8226;z = (0, 0, 1, 0)&#8226;z = 2</text>
  <text x="380" y="276" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">3 &#215; 3 = 9 = 2 &#10003;</text>

  <text x="380" y="310" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">STEP 2 &#8212; constraint w = y &#215; x</text>
  <text x="380" y="334" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13.5" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">(row A)&#8226;z = (0, 0, 1, 0)&#8226;z = 2</text>
  <text x="380" y="354" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13.5" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">(row B)&#8226;z = (0, 1, 0, 0)&#8226;z = 3</text>
  <text x="380" y="374" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13.5" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">(row C)&#8226;z = (0, 0, 0, 1)&#8226;z = 6</text>
  <text x="380" y="400" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">2 &#215; 3 = 6 &#10003;</text>

  <rect x="60" y="412" width="640" height="48" rx="10" fill="#0e1f16" stroke="#5ddc8a" stroke-width="1.8" />
  <text x="380" y="442" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">every constraint: (row A &#8226; z) &#215; (row B &#8226; z) = (row C &#8226; z)</text>

  <line x1="40" y1="486" x2="720" y2="486" stroke="#223049" stroke-width="1" />
  <text x="380" y="510" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="15.5" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">ONE MULTIPLY PER CONSTRAINT</text>
  <text x="380" y="532" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12.5" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">This is the shape of R1CS, a constraint system many ZK proofs use.</text>
</svg>
